This license follows the spirit of Linus Torvalds' original Linux license: a derivative credits the author and the original work, and the derived source is released publicly under the same license. ACVC adds a limit that license did not have: commercial use is not granted.


1. Permission

You may use, study, modify, and distribute ACVC, in whole or in part, for research, study, and personal use, only when all of the following are true:

- the use is not commercial;
- if there is a derivative work, the final product is not a commercial product;
- you keep this notice and credit the author and the original work;
- if you distribute a modification or a derivative work, you release the corresponding source code to the public under this same license.


2. Commercial use

The following is commercial use, even when the recipient pays nothing:

- commercial software, including freeware and freemium;
- use inside a commercial product, service, or activity, or in support of one;
- research or study whose purpose is to produce, improve, or enable commercial software.

This license does not grant that use.


3. Written authorization

Using ACVC in a commercial software project, or in a research or study project whose purpose is to produce commercial software, requires written authorization from the author of ACVC, Samuraisatoshi, at samuraisatoshi@cryptoworld.8shield.net.

Without that authorization, the permission in section 1 does not cover the use. An authorization, when one exists, covers only what it describes.

To purchase a commercial license, make the deposit in section 8 and send the transaction id to samuraisatoshi@cryptoworld.8shield.net. The deposit is not itself the authorization.


4. Derivative works

A derivative work is allowed for research and study when the final product is not a commercial product.

You may distribute a derivative work, or a modified part, only when all three conditions below are met together:

- the work credits Samuraisatoshi as the author of ACVC and identifies ACVC as the original work, with the repository address above;
- copyright notices stay intact; in a partial distribution, the notices of the included parts stay, and new parts carry the notice of whoever wrote them;
- the derived source code is publicly available, at no extra license charge, under this same license and not under another.

Making the code available only on request, for a fee, or behind an access restriction does not satisfy this section.


5. What this license does not grant

This license does not grant a right of commercial use, does not transfer ownership, and does not allow use of the author's name to endorse a derivative work.

Trademarks and the name ACVC remain the author's. A derivative work must not present itself as the original ACVC.


6. No warranty

ACVC is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. The author is not liable for damages arising from use or inability to use, to the extent allowed by applicable law.


7. Acceptance

By using, modifying, or distributing ACVC, you accept this license. If you cannot meet a condition, you do not have the corresponding permission.


